":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of eigenpairs, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0...vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"tolerance","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The residual a Ritz pair must reach, relative as described above.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"maxIterations","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The matrix–vector products each Lanczos run may spend; nil for the limits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"under Throws."}]}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The eigenpairs, in order from that end of the spectrum."}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Component by component: each component’s null vector first (eigenvalue 0, components in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order of their least vertex), then the smallest positive eigenvalues of the components","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"merged. On a component of at least 64 vertices, thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reorthogonalization and locking, the null vector projected out, from a fixed start vector:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on σI − M (σ Gershgorin’s bound) while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on M⁺ by shift-invert, each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"product a conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pair is accepted when its residual is at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" · λ, relative to itself as for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"algebraicConnectivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; the vectors found are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, and each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value is its vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The dense solver on a smaller","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component, or when k is a third of it or more.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"10) for the basis.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"smallest"},{"text":" is in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0...vertexCount"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when given, is at least 1.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Precondition"},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"text":" when a Lanczos run by shift-invert spends ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":" products","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(1,000 when nil), or a conjugate-gradient solve inside it 20,000 + 2n iterations, without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"converging. A run on σI − M hands over to shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"20√n products or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":", whichever is smaller. The dense solver throws as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"laplacianSpectrum"},{"t